DAY 25 – INHERITANCE

1. INHERITANCE

Inheritance is an OOP concept where properties
and methods can be acquired from one class to another.

It helps in code reusability and represents
parent-child relationships between classes.


2. SINGLE INHERITANCE

Single Inheritance means one child class inherits
from one parent class.


3. MULTIPLE INHERITANCE

Multiple Inheritance means a child class inherits
from more than one parent class.


4. MULTILEVEL INHERITANCE

Multilevel Inheritance is a chain of inheritance.

A child class can access methods of its parent
and grandparent classes.


5. HIERARCHICAL INHERITANCE

Hierarchical Inheritance means multiple child
classes inherit from one parent class.


6. HYBRID INHERITANCE

Hybrid Inheritance is a combination of two or
more types of inheritance.


7. MRO – METHOD RESOLUTION ORDER

MRO stands for Method Resolution Order.

It defines the order in which Python searches
for methods in inheritance, especially in
multiple inheritance.


8. super()

super() is used to call the parent class's
methods or constructor from the child class.


KEY TAKEAWAY

Single Inheritance → One parent → One child

Multiple Inheritance → More than one parent

Multilevel Inheritance → Parent → Child → Grandchild

Hierarchical Inheritance → One parent → Multiple children

Hybrid Inheritance → Combination of inheritance types

MRO → Defines the method search order

super() → Accesses parent class methods or constructor